[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Backend Low Level Requirements
UID: GSSC-BACKEND-LOW-LEVEL-REQUIREMENTS
VERSION: 5.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
    PREFIX: None
    VIEW_STYLE: Narrative
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  PROPERTIES:
    PREFIX: GSSC-BLLR-
    VIEW_STYLE: Table
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DERIVED
    TYPE: SingleChoice(True, False)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION_METHOD
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Inspection)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: CHANGE_DRIVER
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: REVIEW_STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Changed, Approved, Baselined)
    REQUIRED: True
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
    ROLE: Refines
    REVERSE_ROLE: Refined By

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-SERVICE-TRANSACTIONS
TITLE: Service Transactions

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USER-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: User Accounts

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-ACCOUNT-ACCESS
TITLE: Account Access

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGIN
TITLE: /login

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-1
TITLE: Login Identifiers
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take a member login as a password together with either a Username or a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member logs in with a password and one account identifier. The identifier is a Username or the Primary Email.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-7
TITLE: Password Match
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL log the member in when the supplied Username or Primary Email matches a member and the supplied password matches that member's stored password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member login succeeds when the identifier locates the member and the password matches the stored password hash. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-11
TITLE: Login Token Lifetime
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take the lifetime of a Login Token from backend configuration. The configured lifetime is a number of days greater than zero. The configured lifetime defaults to seven days.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The time a Login Token remains valid is configuration. The configured lifetime is greater than zero. The configured lifetime defaults to seven days.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGIN-DATA
TITLE: Data Returned

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-8
TITLE: Login Token Issued
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL issue a Login Token in an HTTP cookie on the successful login response when a member login succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful login yields a Login Token that a later challenge can test. The Login Token is delivered in an HTTP cookie on that response.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-309
TITLE: Login Token Cookie Storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store each Login Token for the client as an HTTP cookie.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The HTTP cookie is the Login Token held by the client. Challenge, logout, and authenticated requests use that cookie.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-292
TITLE: Login Token Cookie HttpOnly
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL set the Login Token HTTP cookie so that client script cannot read the cookie value.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
HttpOnly keeps the Login Token out of script-readable storage.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-310
TITLE: Login Token Cookie Secure
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL mark the Login Token HTTP cookie for secure transport only.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Secure limits the cookie to secure transport.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-311
TITLE: Login Token Cookie SameSite
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL set the Login Token HTTP cookie to a lax same-site policy.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
SameSite=Lax limits cross-site sending while allowing normal same-site browser use.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-312
TITLE: Login Token Cookie Path
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL set the Login Token HTTP cookie path to the site root.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Path=/ applies the cookie to the whole site.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-313
TITLE: Login Token Cookie Max-Age
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL set the Login Token HTTP cookie Max-Age to the configured Login Token lifetime in seconds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Max-Age keeps the cookie lifetime aligned with the Login Token lifetime.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGIN-PERSISTENCE
TITLE: Login Token Persistence

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-315
TITLE: Login Token Hash Stored
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a hash of the Login Token when a member login succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend retains a hash of the Login Token for later challenge and logout.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-182
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-316
TITLE: Login Token Row Removed On Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL remove the Login Token row when that member logs out that token.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
After logout the Login Token is ended. Keeping the row has no further use.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-182
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-317
TITLE: Login Token Rows
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store each Login Token hash in a login tokens table. Each row holds the token hash, the user, the issue time, and the expiry time.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The login tokens table is the durable store for Login Token retention across Unified Backend restarts.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-182
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-318
TITLE: Login Token Available After Start
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL make each retained Login Token available for challenge after the Unified Backend starts.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
After a restart, the backend challenges Login Tokens from durable storage. A process-memory-only Login Token would be lost on restart.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-182
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-3
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-319
TITLE: Expired Login Token Rows Removed
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL remove each Login Token row whose expiry time has elapsed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An expired Login Token is no longer a current login. Removing the row clears ended sessions from durable storage.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-182
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGIN-FAILURES
TITLE: Failure Cases

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-2
TITLE: Both Identifiers Invalidated
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a member login that supplies both a Username and a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The login takes one identifier. A login that supplies both a Username and a Primary Email is invalidated.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-3
TITLE: Neither Identifier Invalidated
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a member login that supplies neither a Username nor a Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The login takes one identifier. A login that supplies neither a Username nor a Primary Email is invalidated.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-4
TITLE: Unknown Username Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Username matches no member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Username that matches no member is not a login. The login is forbidden.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-5
TITLE: Unknown Primary Email Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Primary Email matches no member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Primary Email that matches no member is not a login. The login is forbidden.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-6
TITLE: Password Mismatch Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a member login when the supplied Username or Primary Email matches a member and the supplied password does not match that member's stored password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend compares the supplied password with the member's stored password hash. A password that does not match that hash is forbidden. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-1
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-LOGOUT
TITLE: /logout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-10
TITLE: Member Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL end the member login of a Login Token when that member logs out that token. A later challenge of that Login Token reports it as invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member ends a login by logging out that Login Token. After logout, the token no longer represents a valid login.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-314
TITLE: Logout Clears Login Token Cookie
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL clear the Login Token HTTP cookie on the logout response.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Clearing the cookie ends the session transport for that Login Token.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-179
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-CHALLENGE
TITLE: /challenge

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-CHALLENGE-DATA
TITLE: Data Returned

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-9
TITLE: Login Token Challenge
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report a challenged Login Token as valid or invalid. The report is valid for a Login Token issued for a successful member login that has not expired and has not been logged out. The report does not include the contents of the Login Token.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The challenge tells the caller whether the Login Token is valid. The report is only valid or invalid, and it does not return the token contents.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-3
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-12
TITLE: Expired Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL expire a Login Token when its lifetime has elapsed since the token was issued. A later challenge of that Login Token reports it as invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Login Token stops being a valid login when its configured lifetime has elapsed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PASSWORD-MANAGEMENT
TITLE: Password Management

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PASSWORD-CHANGE
TITLE: /password/change

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-224
TITLE: Password Change
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL replace a logged-in member's own password through the password change transaction.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A logged-in member replaces that member's password through this transaction.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-247
TITLE: Password Change Login Token Required
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password change when the request lacks a valid Login Token for that member, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Only a logged-in member may replace that member's password. A valid Login Token identifies that member.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-225
TITLE: Password Change Inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take a password change as the member's current password and the new password.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The current password confirms the caller holds the existing credential. The new password is the replacement.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-226
TITLE: Password Change Current Match
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL replace the member's password when the supplied current password matches that member's stored password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A password change succeeds when the current password matches the stored hash. Separate requirements cover new-password rules.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-227
TITLE: Password Change Current Mismatch
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password change when the supplied current password does not match that member's stored password hash, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A wrong current password must not replace the stored hash.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-228
TITLE: Password Change Differs From Current
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password change when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password matches the member's current password hash, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A replacement password must differ from the current password for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-248
TITLE: Password Change Differs From History
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password change when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password matches any of the last N retained past password hashes, and the backend writes nothing. N is the password history count from backend configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A replacement password must differ from each retained past password for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-229
TITLE: Password History Count Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take the password history count from backend configuration. The configured count is an integer greater than or equal to zero. The configured count defaults to three.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The number of past password hashes the backend retains, and checks on replacement, is configuration and defaults to three.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-230
TITLE: Password Minimum Length Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take the minimum password length from backend configuration. The configured length is an integer greater than zero. The configured length defaults to eight.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The minimum length of a new password is configuration and defaults to eight.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-249
TITLE: Password Minimum Length
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a new password that is shorter than the configured minimum length when the member is not the permanent admin account, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A new password must meet the configured minimum length for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-250
TITLE: Password Required Character Classes
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a new password that omits a capital letter, a lowercase letter, a number, or a special character when the member is not the permanent admin account, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A new password must include each required character class for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-251
TITLE: Password Allowed Characters
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a new password that contains a character outside the allowed set when the member is not the permanent admin account, and the backend writes nothing. The allowed characters are letters, digits, and ` ~ ! @ # $ % ^ & * ( ) _ + - = { } | [ ] \ : " ; ' < > ? , . /
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A new password may use only the allowed characters for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-232
TITLE: Permanent Admin Password Replacement
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL accept a new password for the permanent admin account when that account replaces its password through password change or password recovery.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The permanent admin account may keep a simple configured password. The length, character, and history invalidations apply only to other members.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-233
TITLE: Existing Password Login Validity
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL accept a stored password for member login when that password does not meet the new-password length or character rules.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Password rules apply to replacement. No high-level requirement requires accepting a non-conforming stored password for login, so this login acceptance is derived.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-234
TITLE: Password Change Stores Current Hash
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the new password hash as the member's current password hash when a password change succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful replacement updates the current password hash.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-112
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-252
TITLE: Password Change Retains History
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL retain the previous current password hash in the past password hash history when a password change succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful replacement keeps the previous hash in history. A separate requirement limits how many past hashes the backend keeps.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PASSWORD-RECOVERY-REQUEST
TITLE: /password/recovery-request

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-235
TITLE: Password Recovery Request Input
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take a password recovery request as an email address.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery request identifies the member by an email address.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-236
TITLE: Password Recovery Message Sent
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL send a password recovery message to a member's Primary Email when the recovery request email address matches that Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend sends recovery mail only to a member's Primary Email. Message wording and layout are out of scope.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-237
TITLE: Password Recovery Request Unknown Email Success
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report success for a password recovery request when the supplied email address matches no member Primary Email.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The response does not reveal whether an address is registered. Success here covers only an unknown address.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-273
TITLE: Password Recovery Request Send Success
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report success for a password recovery request when the backend sends the recovery message.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A completed send ends the recovery request with success.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-274
TITLE: Password Recovery Request Send Server Error
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report a server error for a password recovery request when sending the recovery message fails.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An SMTP send failure is a server-side error and is not reported as success.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-238
TITLE: Password Recovery Token Hash Stored
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a hash of the recovery token when the backend sends a recovery message.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend retains a hash of the recovery token for later verification.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-253
TITLE: Password Recovery Token Plaintext Omitted
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL omit the recovery token plaintext from storage.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend stores a hash of the recovery token and does not retain the token itself.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-239
TITLE: Password Recovery Token Lifetime Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take the lifetime of a password recovery token from backend configuration. The configured lifetime is a number of days greater than zero. The configured lifetime defaults to one day.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend expires a recovery token after the configured lifetime. The configured lifetime defaults to one day.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PASSWORD-RECOVERY
TITLE: /password/recover

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-240
TITLE: Password Recovery Inputs
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL take a password recovery as a recovery token, the Primary Email paired with that token, and a new password.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend takes the token, the Primary Email that received it, and the replacement password.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-254
TITLE: Unknown Recovery Token Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password recovery when the recovery token hash is unknown, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An unknown recovery token cannot replace a password.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-255
TITLE: Expired Recovery Token Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password recovery when the recovery token lifetime has elapsed, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An expired recovery token cannot replace a password.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-256
TITLE: Recovery Email Mismatch Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password recovery when the supplied Primary Email does not match the Primary Email paired with that token, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Primary Email in the recovery request must match the Primary Email that received the token.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-257
TITLE: Used Recovery Token Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid a password recovery when the backend has already marked that recovery token as used, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery token may complete recovery only once.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-268
TITLE: Password Recovery Differs From Current
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password recovery when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password matches the member's current password hash, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery password must differ from the current password for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-269
TITLE: Password Recovery Differs From History
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password recovery when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password matches any of the last N retained past password hashes, and the backend writes nothing. N is the password history count from backend configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery password must differ from each retained past password for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-270
TITLE: Password Recovery Minimum Length
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password recovery when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password is shorter than the configured minimum length, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery password must meet the configured minimum length for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-271
TITLE: Password Recovery Required Character Classes
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password recovery when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password omits a capital letter, a lowercase letter, a number, or a special character, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery password must include each required character class for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-272
TITLE: Password Recovery Allowed Characters
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate a password recovery when the member is not the permanent admin account and the new password contains a character outside the allowed set, and the backend writes nothing. The allowed characters are letters, digits, and ` ~ ! @ # $ % ^ & * ( ) _ + - = { } | [ ] \ : " ; ' < > ? , . /
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A recovery password may use only the allowed characters for every member other than the permanent admin account.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-258
TITLE: Password Recovery Stores Current Hash
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the new password hash as the member's current password hash when a password recovery succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful recovery updates the current password hash.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-112
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-259
TITLE: Password Recovery Retains History
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL retain the previous current password hash in the past password hash history when a password recovery succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful recovery keeps the previous hash in history. A separate requirement limits how many past hashes the backend keeps.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-260
TITLE: Password Recovery Marks Token Used
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL mark the recovery token as used when a password recovery succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful recovery consumes the recovery token.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

