[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USER-GET-FAILURES
TITLE: Failure Cases

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-48
TITLE: User Read Missing Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user read when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie is missing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A missing Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-133
TITLE: User Read Unknown Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user read when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie is unknown.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An unknown Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-134
TITLE: User Read Logged-Out Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user read when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie has been logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A logged-out Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-135
TITLE: User Read Expired Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user read when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie has expired.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An expired Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-55
TITLE: User Not Found
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report the user not found when the user read names a cuid that no user has. The report is the same for every logged-in caller.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A cuid that belongs to no user is a missing record. The report is the same for every logged-in caller because a cuid is not private. The test binds this report to HTTP 404. A cuid that exists still returns the allowed fields.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

