[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USER-POST-FAILURES
TITLE: Failure Cases

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-56
TITLE: User Update Missing Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie is missing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A missing Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-166
TITLE: User Update Unknown Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie is unknown.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An unknown Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-167
TITLE: User Update Logged-Out Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie has been logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A logged-out Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-168
TITLE: User Update Expired Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the Login Token in the HTTP cookie has expired.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An expired Login Token is not a current login. The failure does not say which check failed.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-57
TITLE: User Update Not Found
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report the user not found when the user update names a cuid that no user has.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A cuid that belongs to no user is a missing record. The test binds this report to HTTP 404.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-59
TITLE: is administrator User Update
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the caller is not an administrator and the user identified by the cuid is an administrator, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A user who is an administrator can be changed only by an administrator. A user moderator is forbidden from updating an administrator, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-60
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-171
TITLE: User Update Forbidden
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL forbid the user update when the cuid is not the caller's own cuid and the caller is not a user moderator, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A caller who is not a user moderator and is not the identified user is forbidden from updating that user. An administrator is a user moderator.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-34
GSSC5-36
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-173
TITLE: User Update Cuid
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate the user update when the request includes a cuid, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The cuid in the path identifies the user. A cuid in the update body is an invalid field, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-175
TITLE: User Update First Name Empty
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate the user update when an included First Name is "" for a user other than the permanent admin account, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This required field stays non-empty. The permanent admin account may store it empty. An empty value for any other user invalidates the update, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-36
