[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-223
TITLE: Own Membership Status Update
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate the user update when the cuid is the caller's own user and the request includes Membership Status, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member can see their own Membership Status and cannot change it. Including it on that member's own update invalidates the update, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-282
TITLE: Own Position Update
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate the user update when the cuid is the caller's own user, the caller is not an administrator, and the request includes Position, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member's own Position is view-only unless that member is an administrator. Including Position on that member's own update invalidates the update, and the backend writes nothing.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-36
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-84
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-86
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-62
TITLE: Password Hash Unchanged
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL invalidate the user update when the request includes the password hash, and the backend writes nothing. The stored password hash remains the current hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Password replacement uses the password change and recovery transactions. No high-level requirement requires invalidating a user update that includes the password hash, so that invalidation is derived.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-34, GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

