[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-USERS-TABLE-CONSTRAINTS
TITLE: Users Table Constraints

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-18
TITLE: Unique Username
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL associate each Username in the users table with one user.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login treats a Username as locating one user. Each stored Username belongs to one user.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-19
TITLE: Unique Primary Email
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL associate each Primary Email in the users table with one user.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login treats a Primary Email as locating one user. Each stored Primary Email belongs to one user.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-PASSWORD-HISTORY-STORE
TITLE: Password History

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-244
TITLE: Past Password Hash Rows
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store each retained past password hash for a user in a password history table. Each row holds the password hash and links that hash to the user by the user's cuid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend stores past password hashes separately from the current hash and identifies the owning user by cuid.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-262
TITLE: Past Password Hash Creation Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the date and time of password creation on each past password hash row.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The creation date and time identify which past hash is oldest when the history exceeds the configured count.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-261
TITLE: Past Password Hash Count Limit
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL delete the oldest past password hash rows by creation date and time when a user's password history exceeds the configured password history count.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend keeps only the configured number of past password hashes for each user and drops the oldest first.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-113
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BLLR-245
TITLE: Password Recovery Token Rows
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store each password recovery token hash in a password recovery tokens table. Each row holds the token hash, the user, the Primary Email paired with that token, the issue time, the expiry time, and a used marker.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The backend stores recovery token hashes with the Primary Email and lifetime needed to complete recovery.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-35
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-BHLR-161
  ROLE: Refines

